WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Your client wants an AI pilot.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:06.820
First come the interviews, the conflicting answers, and the chase for data.

3
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.630
Then the routine. Discovery calls.

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.270
Chasing stakeholders. Rewriting notes.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.400
Mapping workflows. And waiting on IT for data.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.540
Weeks pass. Then you guess.

7
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.370
Estimate the hours, write the scope, build the deck, and hope the data is there.

8
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.210
Often it isn't.

9
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.770
The data's a mess, the client wants more, and every fix comes out of your margin.

10
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.970
Meet Alyvon. From discovery to building, in days, not weeks.

11
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.510
Send one link.

12
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.490
Stakeholders talk to an AI consultant on their own time.

13
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:48.290
Alyvon brings their needs together and surfaces disagreements for your team to resolve.

14
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.810
With the client's permission, Alyvon checks their systems with read-only access.

15
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.930
You see what data exists and where the gaps are,

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.880
before you commit to a scope.

17
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.950
That evidence becomes the scope of work, delivery plan, and agreed measures of success.

18
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.490
Your team reviews it. The client signs off.

19
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.070
Then the AI workforce builds from the approved plan,

20
00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.040
with your team in control.

21
00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.360
New requests become change orders, not free work.

22
00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.060
Results are tracked against the agreed baseline. Know what to build.

23
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.760
Build what you sold. And bill for the rest.

24
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.680
Alyvon. From discovery to building, in days, not weeks.
